  "findings": [
    "M289, SNL215:028 and HB122 callout10, is the transmission sprocket output shaft; quantity two. M255 is a distinct central cross shaft, quantity one. Do not merge their identities or join their solids.",
    "M292 is the separate track-brake drum, SNL83:036 and HB122 callout7, quantity two. HB122 traces output through M289 to the brake and sprocket; HB149 places the brake immediately inboard of the chain sprocket.",
    "M291 overall axial width four inches and tooth width1.5inches are printed in HB132. Plate22 axial/radial proportions are conditional scales from that control, not independent dimensions. Perspective and local scan distortion remain.",
    "This study keeps the earlier M291 bore and ten rectangular spline grooves to test their interface. The shaft root, spline form, bearing-journal radii, transitions and drum web/rim stock remain reconstruction assumptions. Their fits do not establish original shaft dimensions.",
    "SNL165:013 allocates four M290 retaining rings to the two M289 shafts, plus two to M267. Bearings, rings, axial capture, brake bands and epicyclic planet-disk connection are not populated by this rotor study."
  ],
  "historical_fit_qualified": false
